config VIDEO_EXYNOS_ISPFE
	tristate "Google zumapro ISPFE camera receive complex"
	depends on ARCH_EXYNOS || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on OF
	depends on PM
	help
	  Bring-up driver for BLK_ISPFE on Google's zumapro (Tensor G4): the
	  CSIS links and their combo D/C-PHYs, the ISPFE front end, and the
	  PDMA that carries per-frame descriptors.

	  At this stage the driver powers the block, restores the CMU state
	  that the power domain does not, and reports the identification
	  registers.  It does not stream and registers no V4L2 devices, so it
	  is of no use outside camera bring-up.

	  If unsure, say N.
